<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruhnama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2001</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Book of the Soul</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ruhnama, or 'Book of the Soul', is a book of spiritual and moral guidance, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> history and personal reflection published under the name of Turkmenistan's president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saparmurat-niyazov">Saparmurat Niyazov</a>, with a first volume in 2001 and a second in 2004. It became a pillar of his personality cult: it was compulsory reading in schools, universities and workplaces and was even required for driving tests. Its role was reduced after his death in 2006.</p></div>
